<title>ITALY: BCI raises stake in insurer Assiba.</title>
<headline>BCI raises stake in insurer Assiba.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italy's Banca Commerciale Italiana (BCI) said it had raised its stake in insurer Assiba to 50 percent from 22 percent, making it joint owner of the venture with Assicurazioni Generali.</p>
<p>A BCI statement said BCI had bought an 18 percent stake previously held by insurer RAS and 10 percent held by insurer Toro Assicurazioni, which founded the company with Generali in 1991.</p>
<p>BCI said it was paying 61.4 billion lire in total for the two insurers' stakes.</p>
<p>It said Assiba's premium growth from new policies was more than 70 percent in the first six months of 1997.</p>
<p>--Milan bureau +392 66129507</p>
</text>
